GOOSELoc modifications to upstream FG² (https://github.com/vita-epfl/FG2),
pinned at commit a55d9d13eb029ab2cccf21cff31b728c78d443b2. Applied by setup.sh.

This is the complete diff between that commit and the FG² tree that trained
the released GOOSELoc checkpoints. It adds an optional `grd_query_bias`
argument to `CVM.forward` (KITTI model); with the default `None` the forward
pass is unchanged, and the camera-only baseline in this directory never sets
it. Everything else (model, losses, Procrustes solver, DINOv2 backbone, config)
is used verbatim. GOOSELoc data handling lives outside the upstream tree, in
data.py.

License: GPL-3.0, like upstream FG².

diff --git a/models/model_kitti.py b/models/model_kitti.py
index de444bc..11feef3 100755
--- a/models/model_kitti.py
+++ b/models/model_kitti.py
@@ -101,11 +101,13 @@ class CVM(nn.Module):
         ### sat
         self.sat_projector =  DeepResBlock_desc(bn, last_dim=desc_dim, in_channels=embed_dim, block_dims=block_dims, add_posEnc=add_posEnc, norm_desc=norm_desc)
     
-    def forward(self, grd_feature, sat_feature, camera_k):
+    def forward(self, grd_feature, sat_feature, camera_k, grd_query_bias=None):
 
         bs = grd_feature.size()[0]
 
         grd_query = self.grd_grid_queries.view(-1, self.embed_dim).unsqueeze(0).repeat(bs, 1, 1)
+        if grd_query_bias is not None:
